WHY

These files are compilations of facts, not works of authorship. The anchor
table states, for each canonical paragraph number, the page of a given printed
edition on which it begins. That is a correspondence between two published
numbering systems: laborious to establish, but discovered rather than invented,
and in most jurisdictions not protected at all. Declaring it free removes the
doubt — and a citation index is of little use if others cannot build on it.

WHICH FILES

  data/anchors.json      canonical paragraph anchors with PDF and printed page
  data/works.json        bibliographic metadata and per-work measures
  data/corpus.json       corpus totals
  data/terms.json        term distributions
  data/keyness.json      log-likelihood profiles
  data/network.json      co-occurrence edges
  data/persons.json      name register
  data/places.json       place register
  data/itinerary.json    the route as given in the memoir
  data/discernment.json  term-family distributions

